\description{
Fits FDA models across multiple environments, accounting for
genotype-by-environment (GxE) interaction on the functional trait
and its relationship to the primary trait of interest. Supports both
two-stage (per-environment profiles then MET model) and single-stage
(joint) approaches, with factor-analytic (FA) variance structures for
modelling GxE.
}
\details{
\subsection{Two-stage approach}{

\strong{Stage 1}: For each environment, \code{\link[=fit_functional_profiles]{fit_functional_profiles()}} extracts
variety-specific B-spline coefficient BLUPs \eqn{\hat{\alpha}_{ve}}.

\strong{Stage 2}: The coefficients are modelled across environments:
\deqn{\hat{\alpha}_{vek} = \mu_k + g_{vk} + (ge)_{vek} + \varepsilon_{vek}}

where:
\itemize{
\item \eqn{g_{vk}} is the variety main effect on coefficient \eqn{k},
\item \eqn{(ge)_{vek}} is the GxE interaction, modelled with an FA structure:
\eqn{\mathrm{var}(\alpha_{v\cdot}) = \Lambda \Lambda' + \Psi},
\item \eqn{\Lambda} is the loadings matrix (environments x factors),
\item and variety scores are the latent factors.
}
}

\subsection{Single-stage approach}{

All environments are fitted simultaneously in a single mixed model:
\itemize{
\item Fixed: intercept + environment + null-space spline terms
\item Random: \code{variety:spline_coef} with \code{fa(environment, k)} variance
\item Spatial: \code{at(environment):ar1(row):ar1(col)} (if requested)
}
}

\subsection{Genomic prediction}{

When \code{genomic_matrix} or \code{pedigree_matrix} is supplied, variety random
effects are modelled as \code{vm(variety, source = G)}, enabling genomic
prediction of unobserved varieties.
}
}
